{title: The Old Rugged Cross}
{title_ko: 갈보리산 위에}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 150장}
{artist: George Bennard}
{genre: Gospel}
{flow: Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: C}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 3/4}
{score: the-old-rugged-cross.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
On a [C]hill far away stood an old rugged [G7]cross
The [G7]emblem of suffering and [C]shame
And I [C]love that old cross where the dearest and [F]best
For a [C]world of lost [G7]sinners was [C]slain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
So I'll [C]cherish the old rugged [G7]cross
Till my [G7]trophies at last I lay [C]down
I will [C]cling to the old rugged [F]cross
And ex[C]change it some [G7]day for a [C]crown
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
O that [C]old rugged cross, so despised by the [G7]world
Has a [G7]wondrous attraction for [C]me
For the [C]dear Lamb of God left His glory a[F]bove
To [C]bear it to [G7]dark Cal[C]vary
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
In the [C]old rugged cross, stained with blood so di[G7]vine
A [G7]wondrous beauty I [C]see
For 'twas [C]on that old cross Jesus suffered and [F]died
To [C]pardon and [G7]sanctify [C]me
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
To the [C]old rugged cross I will ever be [G7]true
Its [G7]shame and reproach gladly [C]bear
Then He'll [C]call me some day to my home far a[F]way
Where His [C]glory for[G7]ever I'll [C]share
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
